oints of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} :step/id #uuid "1d9ba6fc-d1ed-5998-a6a1-15240e008963" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481678}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481736 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "009bebc1-1d70-5146-acb2-345610e6c246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479357} {:answer/id #uuid "662d6cbf-df0b-5a2b-864d-c8e3c7d7c84f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479510} {:answer/id #uuid "872fa692-204b-5b6c-a856-b98e7bca186a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479559} {:answer/id #uuid "8dd16611-f690-5a0f-a18d-5609fa7747fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479569} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0da569-9446-52c8-a13b-44c64c37b563" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479674}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479569} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b9663fd-5968-52a8-ba68-181cef60c992" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "600bd5a7-d330-5937-a607-067ad2bf01ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-71813" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x<2,\\,2<y<4\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,3).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :step/id #uuid "d4a32acc-c162-55a3-84e9-b8804219af5e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481683}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481741 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a79b038c-fe01-5ebc-866e-1019c3411829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460161} {:answer/id #uuid "7e520372-4f2a-52fe-80ef-779b4c47f5ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460162}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460162} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f28ff6b-8064-54e6-ac2a-cbfc20687b92" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460947} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebc8c9ed-7eb1-530d-8dc2-74b72a9c7683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "fals